From: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm660-xiaomi-platina: enable modem + WCN3990 WiFi (direct supplies)

Enable the modem (MSS) remoteproc and the WCN3990 WiFi.

Power the WLAN block with the four rails the stock Android DT of this
exact device uses (icnss node in the live-extracted DT):
  vdd-cx-mx  -> LDO A5  (0.848 V)
  vdd-1.8-xo -> LDO A9
  vdd-1.3-rfa-> LDO A6
  vdd-3.3-ch0-> LDO A19
There is no ch1 rail (the chip reports num_rf_chains = 1, single chain)
and Android drives the rails directly - there is no wcn3990-pmu power
sequencer on this board. This mirrors sdm660-xiaomi-lavender, where WiFi
scan/connect is known to work with the same SoC and firmware generation
(WLAN.HL.1.0.1). A previous revision of this patch modeled a wcn3990-pmu
node with a vddio rail, which does not match the platina hardware; with
it the WLAN firmware crashed (err_qdi.c EX:wlan_process) as soon as a
scan was started.

Signed-off-by: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-platina.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-platina.dts
@@ -913,3 +913,20 @@
 &pm660_rradc {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&remoteproc_mss {
+	firmware-name = "postmarketos/mba.mbn", "postmarketos/modem.mdt";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&wifi {
+	vdd-0.8-cx-mx-supply = <&vreg_l5a_0p848>;
+	vdd-1.8-xo-supply = <&vreg_l9a_1p8>;
+	vdd-1.3-rfa-supply = <&vreg_l6a_1p3>;
+	vdd-3.3-ch0-supply = <&vreg_l19a_3p3>;
+
+	qcom,calibration-variant = "xiaomi_platina";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
